* `hasDerivAt_param_of_jointC`: `ε ↦ Φ ε y` has a genuine derivative at every point of `W`;
* `hasDerivAt_cpdC_param` (**interchange**): `d/dε|_{ε₀} cpdC i (Φ ε) x = cpdC i ψ x` whenever `ψ y` is the
  genuine parameter derivative of `ε ↦ Φ ε y` on the open slice (symmetry of the second derivative);
* `contDiffOn_deriv_slice`: the parameter derivative `y ↦ ∂_ε Φ(ε₀, y)` is `C^∞` on the slice;
* `hasDerivAt_fdir_param`: the first variation of a frame derivative keeps the frame-variation term,
  `δ(D_A f) = Σ_μ b_A^μ ∂_μ f₀ + D_A δf`;
